    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "body": "Each block below is written to test one rule of how a block is drawn. A block written wrongly is still shown, as the text that was typed with a line saying what is wrong.\n\n## A stat takes six figures\n\n```stat | Six figures\nOpen | 12 | in play\nLate | 3 | past their day | bad\nDone this week | 9 | five more than last week | good\nWaiting on you | 2 | to check\nWith an agent | 4 | taken today\nLater | 21 | kept for later\n```\n\n```stat | Seven figures\nOpen | 12 | in play\nLate | 3 | past their day | bad\nDone this week | 9 | five more than last week | good\nWaiting on you | 2 | to check\nWith an agent | 4 | taken today\nLater | 21 | kept for later\nDropped | 5 | let go this month\n```\n\n## Chips need a number and a word\n\n```chips | Chips\nrocket | 4 | launched\nzap |  | shipped\nstar | 7 | \ncheck | 3 | done\n```\n\n## A bar with no number draws no bar\n\n```bar | Hours by project\nKiln | 12 | this week\nPortage | 7 | this week\nSomeday | not measured yet | no figure to draw\n```\n\n## Tone words a colour name stands for\n\n```chips | Tone aliases\ncheck | 1 | written earn | earn\nx | 2 | written danger | danger\ninfo | 3 | written accent | accent\nalert | 4 | written risk | risk\n```\n\n## A block inside a note ends the note\n\n```note | A note\nThis note opens here.\n```stat | Inside the note\nOpen | 12 | in play\n```\n\nThis line is outside the note: the first closing marks after the note opened ended it, and a block cannot sit inside another.\n\n## A ring takes five parts\n\n```ring | Five parts\nRent | 600 | a month\nFood | 300 | a month\nTravel | 120 | a month\nPhone | 40 | a month\nBooks | 30 | a month\n```\n\n```ring | Six parts\nRent | 600 | a month\nFood | 300 | a month\nTravel | 120 | a month\nPhone | 40 | a month\nBooks | 30 | a month\nGifts | 20 | a month\n```",
